/// visible, by user preference.
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `If you wish to supply a NewScreen structure, then you are supplying left/top/width/height information.  This information can be taken from the rectangle resulting from this function: NewScreen.LeftEdge = Rect.MinX; NewScreen.TopEdge = Rect.MinY; NewScreen.Width = STDSCREENWIDTH; /* or ( Rect.MaxX` -
///   Rect.MinX + 1 ) */ NewScreen.Height = STDSCREENHEIGHT; /* or (
///   Rect.MaxY - Rect.Miny + 1 ) */
/// * `Rect -- pointer to a Rectangle structure which this function will fill out with its return values.  Note that to convert a rectangle to a screen "Height" you do (MaxY` -
///   MinY + 1), and similarly for "Width." The rectangle may be passed
///   directly to OpenScreen() as a DisplayClip region (SA_DClip).
///
/// # Returns
/// 0 (FALSE) if the MonitorSpec your NewScreen requests does not exist.
/// Non-zero (TRUE) if it does.
///
/// See also: OpenScreen(), Intuition V36 update documentation
@library("intuition.library")
extern pub fn QueryOverscan(displayID: u32, rect: *Rectangle, oScanType: i16) -> i32
