// Varargs function SetAttrs skipped - needs manual implementation
/// Inquire the value of some attribute of an object. (V36)
///
/// Inquires from the specified object the value of the specified attribute. You
/// always pass the address of a long variable, which will receive the same
/// value that would be passed to SetAttrs() in the ti_Data portion of a TagItem
/// element.
///
/// # Arguments
///
/// # Returns
/// Returns FALSE (0) if the inquiries of attribute are not provided by the
/// object's class.
///
/// See also: NewObject(), DisposeObject(), SetAttrs(), MakeClass(), Document "Basic Object-Oriented Programming System for Intuition" and the "boopsi Class Reference" document.
@library("intuition.library")
extern pub fn GetAttr(attrID: u32, object: *u8, storagePtr: *u8) -> u32
