/// Get a ScreenBuffer for double-buffering. (V39)
///
/// Allocates a ScreenBuffer structure and usually a BitMap. This structure can
/// be used for double (or multiple) buffering in Intuition screens.
///
/// # Arguments
///
/// # Returns
/// Pointer to a valid ScreenBuffer structure, or NULL if failure. You may
/// render into the resulting BitMap as appropriate. You may use the
/// sb_DBufInfo field to access graphics.library ViewPort-buffering
/// features such as learning when it is safe to reuse the previous BitMap.
/// If not, you risk writing into the on-screen BitMap, which can damage
/// menu or gadget rendering!
///
/// See also: FreeScreenBuffer(), ChangeScreenBuffer(), graphics.library/AllocDBufInfo(), graphics.library/ChangeVPBitMap()
@library("intuition.library")
extern pub fn AllocScreenBuffer(sc: *Screen, bm: *BitMap, flags: u32) -> *ScreenBuffer
/// Free a ScreenBuffer structure. (V39)
///
/// Frees a ScreenBuffer structure you got from AllocScreenBuffer(), and
/// releases associated resources. You must call FreeScreenBuffer() before you
/// close your screen.
///
/// # Arguments
///
/// # Returns
/// None.
///
/// See also: AllocScreenBuffer(), ChangeScreenBuffer(), graphics.library/ChangeVPBitMap()
@library("intuition.library")
extern pub fn FreeScreenBuffer(sc: *Screen, consuming sb: *ScreenBuffer)
/// Swap the screen's BitMap. (V39)
///
/// Performs double (or multiple) buffering on an Intuition screen in an
/// Intuition-cooperative manner. The BitMap associated with the supplied
/// ScreenBuffer will be installed in the specified screen, if possible.
///
/// # Arguments
///
/// # Returns
/// Returns non-zero if the operation succeeded. Returns zero if the
/// operation cannot be performed. This function will fail if Intuition's
/// state cannot permit it, for example the user is playing with menus or
/// gadgets.
///
/// See also: AllocScreenBuffer(), FreeScreenBuffer(), graphics.library/ChangeVPBitMap()
@library("intuition.library")
extern pub fn ChangeScreenBuffer(sc: *Screen, sb: *ScreenBuffer) -> u32
/// Depth arrange a screen with extra control. (V39)
